    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for new owners (`POST /api/owners`), formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to the `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it into the GET response. (Not added to `OwnerFields`, so it stays server-assigned, not client-supplied.)\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` to the `owners` table (the DB used by the test profile `hsqldb,spring-data-jpa`).\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 extended the 10 positional seed inserts with a `NULL` for the new column so they still load.\n\n5. **New function `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 reads the built `Owner`, computes `LAST3` as the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, and `NNNN` as `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` zero-padded to 4 digits, then sets it on the entity in place.\n\n6. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignCustomerCode` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `defaultRegistrationDate` and `save`, so the code is computed against the current owner count *before* the new owner is persisted, matching the OfficeFloor function-injection style.\n\nThe global sequence is one more than the current owner count, so consecutive creates get consecutive numbers (e.g. `SMI-0011`, then `JON-0012`), which is exactly what `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` asserts. Full test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures.",
